{"title":"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Remark\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remark</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Shan-Yu and Mulan are playing a game. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be an angle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/2/a12c8cdfce7133f5fef523411a812812cf2ae3c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0^\\circ &lt; \\theta &lt; 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"111\" height=\"16\" /> known to both players. Initially, Shan-Yu makes a paper triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/812a5bf65a623b4fb2fddedb8c99a2b981265d15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{T}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> with measurements of his choice. They repeatedly form the following steps.\n</p>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/812a5bf65a623b4fb2fddedb8c99a2b981265d15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{T}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> has at least one angle measuring exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then the game stops and Mulan wins.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Otherwise, Mulan chooses a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on the perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/812a5bf65a623b4fb2fddedb8c99a2b981265d15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{T}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, different from its three vertices. She then makes a straight cut from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to the opposite vertex of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/812a5bf65a623b4fb2fddedb8c99a2b981265d15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{T}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Shan-Yu discards one of the two triangles. The remaining triangle becomes the new <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/812a5bf65a623b4fb2fddedb8c99a2b981265d15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{T}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>For which real values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can Mulan guarantee her victory in finitely many steps, no matter how Shan-Yu plays?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution\">Video solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YXUCc0KAmyk\">https://youtu.be/YXUCc0KAmyk</a> (by Dedekind Cuts)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>I claim that Mulan must always choose the angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e96243e70d52a9176f4b485c90dc94dc710c1e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\boxed{\\frac{180^\\circ}{n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"85\" height=\"50\" /> for any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/d/d5d874ba60b75e02810ba023ba3f150bb7ad815b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\in \\mathbb{R}_{\\geq 2}^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"66\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>We assume both Shan-Yu and Mulan play optimally. Suppose that the original triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/d/27d0043215602f58422418d1428b67bfe8c3c686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{T}_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> has angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a9874ea56cf8fec1bd246793224fbcfaad17ab3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, none of which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We consider all possible cases of triangles, acute, right, or obtuse. \n</p><p><b>Lemma:</b> The optimal strategy for Mulan is to choose points such that she splits the triangle into two that of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><b>Proof of the Lemma:</b>\n</p><p>If she were to choose a point that is of the properties of Lemma 1, then no matter what triangle Shan-Yu counters, Mulan may always pick the remaining triangle. \n</p><p><b>2026 IMO/Q4:</b>\n</p><p>We now must find all viable theta. If we are able to win against Shan-Yu, then we must come from a direct multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, meaning that one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a9874ea56cf8fec1bd246793224fbcfaad17ab3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This can be quite easily proven. Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/9/219bc2c26775b5acda35df84aef2d1c995804e17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = n\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd, then Mulan may choose a point such that we cut <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/3/d63e25a5c45a801fa4a4bfd719ef9aae57410429.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n-1)\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, in which the result follows from Lemma 1. Otherwise, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> being even is trivial. So, if for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/0/6b07645381f844918783d9f39ed6af01d7c2de0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\in \\mathbb{Z}^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" /> exists and Mulan can obtain it, such a solution is possible. \n</p><p>Now, if Shan-Yu chooses the initial triangle, he will obviously not choose one with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as an angle. However, his angles must sum to 180 degrees. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/5/8950ed675431776018e01822676c3886cc6f029a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180 = k\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" /> for some value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, then Shan-Yu will lose, because if the angle measures of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/812a5bf65a623b4fb2fddedb8c99a2b981265d15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{T}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/f/9ef30b95b7574aa698412edca64d6c2f97a2e922.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z = 180 = k\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"170\" height=\"18\" /> implies that for some placement of points within the triangle, Mulan can form an angle alongside the second line connecting a vertex to a point of her choosing, which yields 180 degrees universally, by precisely choosing a point such that the resulting angles formed are perfect multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>From there, she may repeatedly apply the <b>Lemma</b> to win the game.\n</p><p>Thus, Mulan must always choose the angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e96243e70d52a9176f4b485c90dc94dc710c1e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\boxed{\\frac{180^\\circ}{n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"85\" height=\"50\" /> for any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/d/d5d874ba60b75e02810ba023ba3f150bb7ad815b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\in \\mathbb{R}_{\\geq 2}^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"66\" height=\"24\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/72287b09043ed45b372a517d764e12d07aff8071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> due to the fact that the triangle in question is nondegenerate.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remark\">Remark</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Remark\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>What happens when 180 isn't a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />? Then, she can never apply the Lemma as Shan-Yu will just remove the angled triangle as he will never form a triangle whose angles are multiple measures of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. In addition, as it isn't an integer or nonintegral divisor of 180, she may never form two multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> via a 180 degree angle. Hence, she is at a checkmate, and once again, Shan-Yu, the ruthless leader of the Hun Army, terrorizes the land of math once more.\n</p><p>I have never watched the movie <i>Mulan</i> btw I just did 5 minutes of research. This proof is left as an exercise for the reader. - hahaha\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO\" title=\"2026 IMO\">2026 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competitions_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competitions resources\">Mathematics competitions resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO\" title=\"2026 IMO\">2026 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017172047\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.027 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.043 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 256/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7733/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.018      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.018      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37209:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017172047 and revision id 293485. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}